# What the build stage actually needs is Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, crates/ — and
# crates/mira/ui/dist, which is committed and `include_bytes!`d, so it must NOT
# be excluded here. Everything below is either rebuilt inside the image or has
# nothing to do with it, and every byte of it is a byte uploaded to the daemon
# on each build.

# Several GB of objects for the wrong architecture, and a cache mount inside the
# image already covers incremental rebuilds.
target/

# Blocks. A data directory in the context would be baked into a layer.
data/
mira-data/

.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Agent scratch. Gitignored, so it is invisible to `git status` and easy to
# forget — and a coding agent's worktrees put a full checkout *and* its build
# output in here, which is how a 2.5 GB build context happens on a repository
# whose tracked files are 30 MB.
.claude/

# The docs site and its virtualenv; nothing under docs/ is `include_str!`d.
docs/
site/
.venv-docs/
mkdocs.yml
*.md
!README.md

# The UI is prebuilt and committed. node_modules is ~50 MB of nothing the
# image needs; dist/ beside it is what ships.
crates/mira/ui/node_modules/
crates/mira/ui/.svelte-kit/

# Release-pipeline scratch. release.yml downloads the matrix tarballs into
# artifacts/ and unpacks only the two Linux binaries into dist/linux/<arch>/,
# which is the one thing here the image does want.
artifacts/
*.cdx.json
SHA256SUMS

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
